test("materialization aggregates primary and cleanup failures", async () => { const source=await gitFixture(false), root=await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(),"loom-aggregate-")), target=join(root,"candidate"), child=await import("node:child_process"), {promisify}=await import("node:util"), real=promisify(child.execFile), errors=[]; try { await writeFile(join(source,"x"),"changed"); const fake=async (command,args,options={}) => { if(args.includes("apply")) throw (errors[0]=Error("PRIMARY")); if(args.includes("remove")) throw (errors[1]=Error("CLEANUP")); if(args.includes("list")) return {stdout:`worktree ${target}\nHEAD abc\n\n`}; return real(command,args,options); }; await assert.rejects(()=>materializeCandidate(source,target,fake),error=>error instanceof AggregateError&&error.errors[0]===errors[0]&&error.errors[1]===errors[1]); } finally { await rm(source,{recursive:true,force:true}); await rm(root,{recursive:true,force:true}); } });

test("CLI cleans both acquired worktrees after candidate assertion failure",async()=>{const cleaned=[],removed=[],base={dir:"/owned/b",ref:"v1",commit:"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567",dirty:false,advisory:false,ownership:{}},candidate={dir:"/owned/c",repo:"/candidate-repo",ref:"HEAD",commit:"1123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567",dirty:false,advisory:false,ownership:{},diffDigest:"d"};let assertions=0;await assert.rejects(()=>runEvaluationCli([],{cwd:"/repo",requestApproval:async()=>evalApproval(),resolveOmpExecutable:async()=>"/opt/omp",exec:async()=>({stdout:"omp/"+OMP.version}),assertCandidate:async()=>{if(assertions++)throw Error("AFTER_CANDIDATE");return candidate},mkdtemp:async()=>"/owned",materializeBaseline:async()=>base,materializeCandidate:async()=>candidate,cleanupWorktree:async owner=>cleaned.push(owner),rm:async dir=>removed.push(dir)}),/AFTER_CANDIDATE/);assert.deepEqual(cleaned.map(x=>x.dir),["/owned/candidate","/owned/baseline"]);assert.deepEqual(removed,["/owned"])});

test("eval redaction boundary covers structured raw credentials and local paths",()=>{const input={apiKey:"a", "x-api-key":"b",GITHUB_TOKEN:"c",AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY:"d",client_secret:"e",private_key:"f",service_API_KEY:"g",myPassword:"h",sessionId:"i",authToken:"j",nested:'Authorization: Basic YmFk x-api-key: raw Cookie: sid=cookie\nSet-Cookie: auth=set token=plain client_secret:"quoted" https://user:pass@example.com/x /opt/private/file ../secret/file C:\\Users\\me\\file relative\\windows\\file',prose:"workspace/file is ordinary prose",ref:"refs/heads/main"};const out=redact(JSON.stringify(input)),parsed=JSON.parse(out);for(const key of ["apiKey","x-api-key","GITHUB_TOKEN","AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY","client_secret","private_key","service_API_KEY","myPassword","sessionId","authToken"])assert.equal(parsed[key],"<REDACTED>",key);for(const leak of ["YmFk","x-api-key: raw","sid=cookie","auth=set","plain","quoted","user:pass","/opt/private","../secret","C:\\Users","relative\\windows"])assert.equal(out.includes(leak),false,leak);assert.equal(parsed.prose,"workspace/file is ordinary prose");assert.equal(parsed.ref,"refs/heads/main")});

test("comparison CLI blocks confirmation boundaries and accepts strict no-confirm packets", async () => {
  const root = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), "loom-frontier-cli-"));
  try {
    const script = join(import.meta.dirname, "compare-frontier.mjs");
    const identity = { ompVersion: OMP.version, generator: OMP.generator, judge: OMP.judge, rubricVersion: OMP.rubricVersion, tier: "quick", runId: "cli-fixture", arms: ["baseline", "candidate"] };
    const makeRow = arm => ({ schemaVersion: 1, kind: "generator", identity: { caseId: "cli-frontier", trial: 1, arm, runId: identity.runId, generator: OMP.generator, judge: OMP.judge, rubricVersion: OMP.rubricVersion, tier: "quick", baselineCommit: "a", candidateCommit: "b", baselineRef: "v", candidateRef: "HEAD", observedVersion: OMP.version }, safety: { pass: true, receipt: { pass: true, labels: [] }, casePass: true, labelsValid: true }, quality: null, evidence: ["fixture"], judge: null, transportBlocked: false });
    const baseline = { identity, rows: [makeRow("baseline")] }, candidate = { identity, rows: [makeRow("candidate")] }, evidence = [...baseline.rows, ...candidate.rows];
    const carrierEvidence = ["omp", "claude", "opencode", "codex"].map(carrier => ({ carrier, Result: ["omp", "claude"].includes(carrier) ? "PASS" : "N/A", Changed: "isolated", Check: "native", "Next action": "retain" }));
    const boundary = { requiresConfirmation: true, target: "repo", scope: "frontier", effects: ["compare"] };
    const canonical = value => value === null || typeof value !== "object" ? value : Array.isArray(value) ? value.map(canonical) : Object.fromEntries(Object.keys(value).sort().map(key => [key, canonical(value[key])]));
    const consent = { confirmed: true, previewDigest: hash(JSON.stringify(canonical({ question: "Which option should be used?", target: boundary.target, scope: boundary.scope, effects: boundary.effects, boundary }))), target: boundary.target, scope: boundary.scope, effects: boundary.effects, currentInteractionMarker: "cli-interaction", confirmedAt: 1000 };
    const factBase = { fact: "fixture", source: "host-native fixture" };
    const facts = { schemaVersion: 1, workerId: "worker-fixture", runId: identity.runId, caseId: "cli-frontier", carrier: "omp", ...factBase, startedAt: 100, finishedAt: 200, status: "PASS", evidenceDigest: hash(JSON.stringify(canonical(factBase))) };
    facts.packetBinding = hash(JSON.stringify(canonical({ question: "Which option should be used?", decisionBoundary: boundary, consent: null, baseline, candidate, evidence, carrierEvidence, fact: factBase })));
    const packet = join(root, "packet.json"); await writeFile(packet, JSON.stringify({ schemaVersion: 1, question: "Which option should be used?", decisionBoundary: boundary, baseline, candidate, evidence, carrierEvidence, factEvidence: facts }));
    const run = args => spawnSync(process.execPath, [script, ...args], { cwd: root, encoding: "utf8" });
    const required = run(["--comparison-packet", packet]); assert.equal(required.status, 2, required.stderr); assert.match(required.stdout, /current human consent packet/);
    const replayed = JSON.parse(await readFile(packet, "utf8")); replayed.consent = consent; await writeFile(packet, JSON.stringify(replayed)); const blocked = run(["--comparison-packet", packet]); assert.equal(blocked.status, 2); assert.match(blocked.stdout + blocked.stderr, /replayable consent is not accepted/);
    const noConfirmBoundary = { type: "confirmation-not-required" };
    facts.packetBinding = hash(JSON.stringify(canonical({ question: "Which option should be used?", decisionBoundary: noConfirmBoundary, consent: null, baseline, candidate, evidence, carrierEvidence, fact: factBase })));
    await writeFile(packet, JSON.stringify({ schemaVersion: 1, question: "Which option should be used?", decisionBoundary: noConfirmBoundary, baseline, candidate, evidence, carrierEvidence, factEvidence: facts }));
    const valid = run(["--comparison-packet", packet]); assert.equal(valid.status, 0, valid.stderr); assert.match(valid.stdout, /"result":"PASS"/);
    for (const args of [["--unknown"], ["--tier", "quick", "--tier", "full"], ["stray"], ["--comparison-packet"]]) { const result = run(args); assert.equal(result.status, 2, args.join(" ")); assert.match(result.stdout + result.stderr, /BLOCKED/); }
  } finally { await rm(root, { recursive: true, force: true }); }
});
